## Whole-code relocation bound

Moving all 2,480 remaining resident service bytes, while retaining the PSP, stack and all mutable state, leaves at least 1,184 paragraph-rounded low bytes. The optimistic release is at most 2,480 bytes before new gateways, bindings or stacks.
This assumes packed low storage with no retained code hole. Separate environment/batch allocations are unchanged; existing high catalogs and code earn no additional credit. This is not a linked relocated implementation or a measured saving.

